  "body": "## Release 0.22.0\n\nThis PR holds the release branch of v0.22.0. The maintainer ordered this cut.\n\n## Start condition\n\n- Cut start: 2026-11-16T10:18Z.\n- `main` at the start: `f90e9dc8ecd32a17d5a0379ff7d52f040a3c9d69`. The previous tag is `v0.21.0`.\n- Open `P1` issues: none.\n- Open `P2` issues: #2004 only. The maintainer released #2004 for this cut on 2026-11-16 (\"Cut without #2004\"): https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/2004#issuecomment-6913297037\n- #2004 is under \"Known issues\" in the release notes. Its fix is in PR #2013 and ships in the next minor.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `RECOMMENDED.md`: `cargo xtask decisions --version 0.22.0` gathered 58 decision files under the `v0.22.0` heading and removed them from `docs/decisions/`.\n- `RELEASE_NOTES.md`: a new 0.22.0 section is on top. The older sections are below it and do not change.\n- `CHANGELOG.md`: 42 rows for the behaviour PRs that merged since `v0.21.0`.\n- `Cargo.toml` and `Cargo.lock`: the version is 0.22.0 (`cargo xtask release --version 0.22.0 --no-tag --skip-gate`).\n\n## Breaking\n\nPR #2026 (#1453) is breaking: the project file format goes from 61 to 62. Older builds refuse a file that 0.22.0 saves. The release notes say this first. While the major is 0, this bumps MINOR.\n\n## Upgrade note\n\nAfter the upgrade, each saved operation shows as out of date one time. Generate it again before a post (PR #2155, issue 2152).\n\n## Checks\n\n- `cargo check -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui -j 6`: pass on this branch.\n- The release gate (`cut.yml`, stage `gate`) is not started here. The maintainer starts it.\n- Pixel snapshots: skipped in this cut. The maintainer decided that they have no value. No PNG changed.\n- The Windows arms of the per-OS pinned readings did not run.\n\nChangelog: none (release mechanics)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
